 =========================================================
   CSS NOTES: Common Pseudo-Classes

   Pseudo-classes are used to define a special state of an element.
   They start with a colon (:)

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :hover
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies when the user places the mouse over an element.

   Example:
   button:hover {
     background-color: blue;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :active
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies when an element is being clicked.

   Example:
   button:active {
     transform: scale(0.95);
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :focus
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies when an input or element is focused (clicked or tabbed).

   Example:
   input:focus {
     border-color: green;
   }

  -> Only focusable elements can get focus:

        inputs

        buttons

        links

Headings (h1–h6) are not focusable by default

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :disabled
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies to form elements that are disabled.

   Example:
   input:disabled {
     background-color: lightgray;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :enabled
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies to form elements that are enabled by default.

   Example:
   input:enabled {
     border: 2px solid black;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :placeholder-shown
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies when an input is showing placeholder text.

   Example:
   input:placeholder-shown {
     border-color: red;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :visited
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Applies to links that have already been visited.

   Example:
   a:visited {
     color: purple;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :first-of-type
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Selects the first element of its type among siblings.

   Example:
   p:first-of-type {
     color: blue;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :last-of-type
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Selects the last element of its type among siblings.

   Example:
   p:last-of-type {
     color: red;
   }

   ---------------------------------------------------------
   :nth-of-type(n)
   ---------------------------------------------------------
   Selects elements based on position of the same type.

   Example:
   li:nth-of-type(2) {
     font-weight: bold;
   }

   Summary:
   Pseudo-classes style elements based on state, position,
   or user interaction.
